# Response headers for every asset this site serves.
#
# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets reads this file from the root of the uploaded directory.
# @astrojs/cloudflare appends its own `/_astro/*` immutable-cache rule to whatever is here, so
# both rules end up in dist/client/_headers and both apply.
#
# ─── the CSP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `{{INLINE_SCRIPT_HASHES}}` is a build-time placeholder. scripts/build-headers.mjs replaces it
# with a `'sha256-…'` for every distinct inline <script> in the built HTML, computed from the
# real output, and scripts/check-headers.mjs then fails the build if any inline script in dist
# is not covered. Hard-coding the hashes here instead would be unmaintainable: Astro inlines the
# bundled component scripts (the theme toggle, the part table of contents, the agency table's
# filter and sort), so their hashes change with any edit to those components. Deriving them from
# the output is the only version that cannot silently drift out of date.
#
# If the placeholder ever survives into a deploy, the CSP degrades safely — an unrecognised
# source expression is ignored, leaving `script-src 'self'`, which blocks the inline scripts and
# loses the progressive enhancement rather than opening a hole. The build fails first.
#
# `style-src` carries 'unsafe-inline' and that is a deliberate, bounded exception. The bar charts
# and the amendment timeline set a computed width/height in a `style` attribute — that is how the
# chart geometry is laid out in the same paint as the text, which is what keeps CLS at zero. CSP
# hashes do not cover style ATTRIBUTES, only <style> blocks, and there are no <style> blocks in
# the output at all. `style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'` would be the tighter spelling, but Firefox
# does not implement `style-src-attr` and falls back to `style-src`, which would leave every bar
# chart collapsed for Firefox readers. No inline style value on this site contains anything but a
# percentage or a rem length computed at build time from our own data.
#
# Everything else is 'none' or 'self': the site has no images, no web fonts, no forms, no frames,
# and makes no network requests after load. In particular it never talks to ecfr.gov from a
# reader's browser — `connect-src 'self'` makes that a browser-enforced property of the deployed
# site, not just a convention in the source.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self' {{INLINE_SCRIPT_HASHES}}; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
